# Django

## Layout

- One app per business capability (not per technical layer)
- Project package = settings, root URLs, ASGI/WSGI only — no domain models/views there
- Custom user model from day one if auth exists
- Settings from environment; fail fast on missing production secrets

## Models

- Singular PascalCase models; `snake_case` field names
- Field order: DB fields → relationships → `Meta` → `__str__` → properties → methods
- Put single-model query/logic on managers/querysets; multi-model writes and side effects in services

```python
# ❌ BAD — fat view
def create_order(request):
    order = Order.objects.create(user=request.user)
    order.total = sum(...)
    order.save()
    send_email(order)
    return redirect(order)

# ✅ GOOD — thin view + service
def create_order(request):
    order = order_create(user=request.user, items=…)
    return redirect(order)
```

## Views & services

- First view arg is always `request`
- Views: parse input, authz, call service/selector, return response
- `services.py` = writes / use-cases; `selectors.py` = optimized reads (optional until needed)
- Prefer explicit `related_name`; avoid N+1 (`select_related` / `prefetch_related`)
- Migrations: never edit applied migrations; data migrations for backfills; no in-place destructive type changes without expand/contract
